1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,855
Hi, I'm Isiaq Tijani, a solo builder from Ibadan,

2
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:04,600
Nigeria.

3
00:00:05,287 --> 00:00:07,075
I'm a biochemist by training.

4
00:00:07,712 --> 00:00:10,505
I graduated with first class from an Arabic college,

5
00:00:10,525 --> 00:00:13,100
I've written books, and I teach biochemistry.

6
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:15,775
I taught myself to build software,

7
00:00:15,838 --> 00:00:18,793
and over the past months I've built several AI-agent and on-chain

8
00:00:18,813 --> 00:00:19,587
products.

9
00:00:21,268 --> 00:00:22,630
Now I'm building VOID.

10
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:26,235
Today, if you let an AI agent spend your money,

11
00:00:26,255 --> 00:00:27,755
you have two bad options.

12
00:00:28,456 --> 00:00:30,056
Give it a wallet and hope.

13
00:00:30,768 --> 00:00:34,118
Or approve every step, and then it's not really an agent.

14
00:00:34,843 --> 00:00:36,305
VOID is a third option.

15
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,168
You set a policy:

16
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:41,818
how much, for how long, and the one contract the agent may call.

17
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,505
A smart contract enforces it.

18
00:00:45,218 --> 00:00:48,293
Outside the policy, the agent simply cannot act.

19
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,430
I didn't just say that, I tested it.

20
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:56,555
I told a real AI agent it was hijacked and to drain a vault.

21
00:00:57,267 --> 00:00:59,055
It tried five different ways.

22
00:00:59,755 --> 00:01:01,710
The contract rejected all five,

23
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:04,730
on-chain, with real transactions anyone can open.

24
00:01:05,405 --> 00:01:07,492
Only the action I approved went through.

25
00:01:08,192 --> 00:01:10,255
You can replay that run on our site.

26
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:12,715
Why me?

27
00:01:13,465 --> 00:01:15,820
First, I hit this problem myself,

28
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,703
every time I gave an agent a key.

29
00:01:18,403 --> 00:01:20,778
Second, I ship the whole thing alone:

30
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:24,553
contracts, API, app and demo, in about ten days.

31
00:01:25,228 --> 00:01:28,465
Third, as a teacher, I explain hard things simply,

32
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:31,740
and as a scientist, I design tests that could prove me wrong.

33
00:01:33,352 --> 00:01:36,094
It's testnet only, on Base and Arbitrum,

34
00:01:36,114 --> 00:01:37,439
and not audited yet.

35
00:01:38,177 --> 00:01:41,414
Next, I want a pilot with a few agent builders.

36
00:01:42,077 --> 00:01:42,664
VOID:

37
00:01:42,702 --> 00:01:46,039
session keys for agents that the contract itself enforces.

38
00:01:46,727 --> 00:01:47,402
Thank you.
